.TH "bead redact" 1  "bead redact " 
.SH NAME
bead redact \- Redact one historical secret by scanner fingerprint
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbead redact\fR [\fB\-\-actor\fR] [\fB\-\-reason\fR] [\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR] [\fB\-\-json\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-finding\fR|\fB\-\-resume\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Destroy exactly one sensitive byte range selected by a current secret\-scanner fingerprint.
.PP
The command never accepts or prints the matched value. A new redaction requires
\-\-finding, \-\-actor, and \-\-reason. Fingerprints from either live rows or retained
current/previous checkpoint issue records are accepted. The service derives the
live row from a checkpoint record and revalidates the fingerprint against those
live bytes under the maintenance and checkpoint\-publication locks, replaces only
that range with the fixed bead\-rs marker, records a nonsecret receipt, and
publishes a sanitized checkpoint generation set. Publication is mandatory even
when workspace automatic publication is disabled.
.PP
If publication fails after the SQLite redaction commits, no semantic mutation is
repeated. Resume the recorded receipt with `bead redact \-\-resume RECEIPT_ID`.
.PP
EXAMPLES:
  bead doctor \-\-scope secrets \-\-format json
  bead redact \-\-finding FINGERPRINT \-\-actor operator \-\-reason "credential rotation" \-\-dry\-run \-\-json
  bead redact \-\-finding FINGERPRINT \-\-actor operator \-\-reason "credential rotation" \-\-json
  bead redact \-\-resume RECEIPT_ID \-\-json
.PP
EXIT CODES:
  0  redaction and sanitized publication completed, or dry\-run succeeded
  1  internal failure or redaction committed but publication did not complete
  2  invalid request, actor, reason, fingerprint, or option combination
  3  finding or receipt not found
  4  stale target or semantic conflict
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-finding\fR \fI<FINGERPRINT>\fR
Live or retained\-checkpoint fingerprint reported by secret diagnostics
.TP
\fB\-\-resume\fR \fI<RECEIPT_ID>\fR
Resume sanitized publication for an already committed receipt
.TP
\fB\-\-actor\fR \fI<ACTOR>\fR
Identity ordering a new redaction
.TP
\fB\-\-reason\fR \fI<REASON>\fR
Bounded nonsecret justification for a new redaction
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Report the exact selector and effects without changing SQLite or checkpoint files
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Emit the preview or published receipt as JSON
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
